.TH ASCIIORGAN 1
.SH NAME
asciiorgan \- keyboard organ
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/asciiorgan
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ASCIIOrgan
is a keyboard organ and ASCII chart.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A 32-row chart lists the codes 00\-7F in hex with each printable
character shown in red.
Every keypress re-pitches a continuous drone, one semitone per
ASCII code
.RB ( freq
=
440\(mu2\u\s-2(ch\-1B\-49)/12\s+2\d
Hz, as TempleOS
.BR Snd(ch-CH_ESC) ),
so adjacent codes are adjacent notes and the tone sustains until the
next key.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B any key
Sound that key's semitone, held until the next key
.TP
.B Esc
Silence the drone and quit
.PD
.PP
Clicking the organ sprite at the bottom launches
.IR psalmody (1),
the ``better organ'' the original links to.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/asciiorgan.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR psalmody (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
Shift-Esc is indistinguishable from Esc here; both silence and exit,
as in the original.
